Core Concepts
Agents
Configurable payment entities with a defined purpose, spend limits, and tool permissions.
Payment Intents
Every payment starts as an intent — a recorded request before execution, enabling audit and approval.
Intent Verification
A separate model scores each payment intent against the conversation and agent purpose. Low scores pause the payment for human approval.
Tool Permissions
Control which banking operations an agent can execute — automatically or with approval.
Spend Limits
Hard and soft limits on per-transaction, daily, and monthly spending.
Approvals
Real-time human-in-the-loop approval flows for tool calls and spend limit overrides.
